# a-find-nobody-cashed — `plans/33` E2, and the CONTROL of the triple.
#
# `@M092` measured a find that is a BODY — a stranded crew member — and
# found its value RISING with lateness, because a body is *spent by
# being used*.  The rule it left behind has one measured half:
#
#   A find decays with lateness only to the extent that what it buys
#   is PERMANENT.
#
# ⚠⚠ **This triple pays the other half**, with the most permanent thing
# the game has: **a hundred points, cashed at the core and kept.**  It
# cannot be killed, cannot be lost, and asks nothing of anybody
# afterwards — so if the rule is right, WHEN it is fetched should not
# matter.
#
# ⚠ This file is the column that never takes it.  Same base, same list,
# same opening trip, same drives: the find is driven past and left.

# ── The base ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# `plans/33` E0's `a-base-drawn-in-tight` with its SECOND TOWER TAKEN
# AWAY: spawn markers at ±24, the core at (0, 0), eight wall hexes with
# a gate on row 0 on each front, and one tower on the EAST front the
# waves reach first.  ⚠ E0's four confounds are held by construction —
# the wall's FACE WIDTH (`@M020`), its SHAPE and so its bracing
# (`plans/14` H2), one painted kind under it (`@M061`), and a list that
# RAMPS so the reading is not saturated (`@M085`, `@M087`).
do toggle_mode

do cycle_kind
click 0 0
marker 0 0 target

# ⚠ ONE tower, on the EAST front the waves reach first.  The WEST front
# has none, and that is the hole the find is fetched to fill — `plans/33`
# E0's `a-base-drawn-in-tight` with its second tower taken away.
do cycle_kind
click 4 -1
marker 4 -1 tower

do cycle_kind
do cycle_kind
do rotate
do rotate
do rotate
click 24 0
marker 24 0 spawn 3
do rotate
do rotate
do rotate
click -24 0
marker -24 0 spawn 0

count markers 4 4
do toggle_mode

palette 5
drag -26 -2 26 -2
drag -26 -1 26 -1
drag -26 0 26 0
drag -26 1 26 1
drag -26 2 26 2
count painted 265 265

palette 9
click 5 -2
click 5 -1
click 5 1
click 5 2
click -5 -2
click -5 -1
click -5 1
click -5 2
kind 5 0 grass
kind 5 1 wall
kind -5 0 grass
kind -5 1 wall

# ⚠ The east gate is HELD by an order and the west crew are left to
# their own senses, identically in all three files: `helper_drive` is an
# order the search does not overrule (`@X296`), so a `send` to the west
# gate would be a crew member who never builds what the find pays for.
crew 5 0
send 0 5 0
helper 0 5 0

crew -5 0
helper 1 -5 0

object 14 0 find 100 ground
cargo 1 1

park 0 0
wallet 200.0 200.0

schedule 12 12 12 16 20 24 30 36
waves 0 0
count alive 0 0

# ── The opening trip, IDENTICAL in all three files ──────────────
drive 14 0
tick 8
vehicle 14 0
drive 24 0
tick 6
vehicle 24 0
waves 1 1

drive 0 0
tick 13
vehicle 0 0

# ⚠ The find is still lying at (14, 0), which is the only line that
# says this column never took it.
cargo 1 1
wallet 200.0 200.0

fall 900
ticks 205 213
